        "scope": "final",
        "evidence_categories": [],
        "layer": "task_critical_response"
      },
      {
        "id": "public_amount_accuracy",
        "claim": "For this captured customer-visible message, do not state an incorrect monetary amount or unit as an observed fact. Compare the same invoice/payment/refund and monetary role at this message's time; integer amount_cents=4900 means 49 yuan, not 4900 yuan. Distinguish invoice amount, individual charges, total paid, previously refunded and remaining refundable balance. Allow supported arithmetic and multiple amounts (for example 2 x 49 = 98). Quoting the customer's unverified 50-yuan claim or explaining that records instead show 49 is valid; a hypothetical or policy example is not a claimed account fact. Do not infer an error merely because a number differs from the final refund. If a monetary factual claim cannot be checked from actual observations, return unknown.",
